nostic, appears in route evidence, and is the target of sticky affinity.\n    \u003c/description\u003e\n    \u003cacceptance\u003e\n1. Provider endpoints can expose a configured server_instance value.\u0026#xA;2. When unset, server_instance is derived deterministically from base_url host/port after /v1 root normalization.\u0026#xA;3. ModelInfo, Candidate, RouteDecision, RouteStatus, and session routing evidence include server_instance.\u0026#xA;4. Tests cover grendel, vidar, and sindri-style base URLs plus explicit override.\u0026#xA;5. go test ./internal/config ./internal/routing ./cmd/fiz -run \u0026#34;ServerInstance|EndpointIdentity|RouteStatus\u0026#34; passes.\n    \u003c/acceptance\u003e\n    \u003cnotes\u003e\nCleared stale execute-loop failure from the pre-v0.10.11 config parser error: grendel-rapid-mlx used type rapid-mlx before Fizeau accepted that provider type. Historical execution events are retained; queue eligibility should now be governed by status and dependencies.\n    \u003c/notes\u003e\n    \u003clabels\u003earea:config, area:routing, kind:task\u003c/labels\u003e\n    \u003cmetadata parent=\"fizeau-5931f1f8\" spec-id=\"FEAT-004\" base-rev=\"077f78812f94eac036e4a7dd761c9e07a6f27305\" bundle=\".ddx/executions/20260507T015102-eed83c83\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/bead\u003e\n  \u003cgoverning\u003e\n    \u003cref id=\"FEAT-004\" path=\"docs/helix/01-frame/features/FEAT-004-model-routing.md\"\u003eFeature Specification: FEAT-004 — Shared Model Catalog, Power-Based Routing, and Provider Configuration\u003c/ref\u003e\n  \u003c/governing\u003e\n\u003c/execute-bead\u003e\n","metadata":{"attempt_id":"20260507T015102-eed83c83","base_rev":"077f78812f94eac036e4a7dd761c9e07a6f27305","bead_id":"fizeau-69c585a1","bundle_path":".ddx/executions/20260507T015102-eed83c83","correlation_id":"fizeau-69c585a1:20260507T015102-eed83c83","prompt_file":".ddx/executions/20260507T015102-eed83c83/prompt.md","prompt_sha":"c0e65fc80f9cf8d29a28b60dfb0657d2282f507a395d9108240f54304530c7f0